{"type": "final", "turn": 3, "content": "\n\nScored the run (OlmoEarth-v1-FT-AWF-Base, 16,384 valid windows on a 128x128 grid, no nodata) and set up a **confidence-stratified** sampling design for your 300 labels.\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Design | confidence (5 strata by margin), budget 300 |\n| Population | 16,384 windows, majority-class grade |\n| Allocation per stratum | 106 / 79 / 47 / 34 / 34 |\n| To-label CSV | `...B4/cluster/3/workspace/design_scores_8f3527f9_confidence_300_s0_to_label.csv` |\n| Design file | `design_scores_8f3527f9_confidence_300_s0.json` |\n\nHow to finish:\n1. For each of the 300 windows in the CSV's order, set `wrong = 1` if the map's class (`map_class`) doesn't match the ground, else `0`. Optionally add the true class id (`reference_class`) for per-class accuracy.\n2. Send me the filled list (or path) and I'll call `olmoearth_estimate_map_error` \u2014 it returns the error rate with the interval this stratified design actually earns (not a plain p \u00b1 1.96 formula).\n\nWant me to re-list any window's row/col or map class while you label?", "forced_by_turn_cap": false, "grounding_revised": false, "seq": 4, "t": 25.34, "seconds": 7.36}
